      "title": "Identify the contract and the payment",
      "narration": "Rosa bought a deferred annuity in her own name with money on which she already paid income tax. It is outside an individual retirement account or employer retirement plan. This is a nonqualified annuity for our examples. Its growth generally can accumulate without annual income tax while held by an individual, but access to the money can create taxable income. Before calculating anything, identify the owner, the contract's issue date and whether the payment is a withdrawal, full surrender or annuity income. Different rules apply to different events. A personal annuity does not become an individual retirement account merely because Rosa intends to use it during retirement.",
