      "title": "A partial withdrawal normally reaches earnings first",
      "narration": "Rosa's teaching contract was issued in twenty twenty, has ninety thousand dollars of cash value and sixty thousand dollars of adjusted investment in the contract. There are no prior distributions or special adjustments. The difference is thirty thousand dollars of gain. Before the annuity starting date, an ordinary partial withdrawal from this contract generally takes taxable earnings before recovering investment. A twenty thousand dollar withdrawal is therefore entirely taxable ordinary income because thirty thousand dollars of gain is available. Do not divide the withdrawal in proportion to premiums and growth. Also do not copy the ordinary basis-first withdrawal treatment from a non-modified life insurance policy.",
