      "title": "Only the amount beyond available gain recovers basis",
      "narration": "Now return to the original ninety thousand dollar value and sixty thousand dollar investment, without making the earlier withdrawal. This time Rosa withdraws forty thousand dollars. The first thirty thousand dollars uses the available gain and is taxable. The remaining ten thousand dollars recovers investment without being taxed again. Her remaining investment is fifty thousand dollars under these simplified facts. The withdrawal is not forty thousand dollars of taxable gain, because the contract contained only thirty thousand dollars of gain. Nor is the entire payment a tax-free return of premiums. Establish the value, adjusted investment and actual transaction amount before choosing the taxable portion.",
