      "title": "Full surrender uses the actual surrender transaction",
      "narration": "A full surrender ends the contract and returns its remaining surrender proceeds. Suppose the insurer states that Rosa would receive eighty-five thousand dollars after all applicable surrender charges, and her unrecovered investment is sixty thousand dollars. Assume no debt or other tax adjustment. The resulting taxable gain is twenty-five thousand dollars. That calculation uses the stated net proceeds for this full surrender. It should not be confused with the partial-withdrawal rule, where gain generally uses cash value before surrender charges. Read whether the question describes a partial payment or complete termination. The same displayed account value does not make those two transactions identical.",
